<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan M2+CD money supply up 3.1 pct yr/yr -- BOJ.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan M2+CD money supply up 3.1 pct yr/yr -- BOJ.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan&quot;s broadly defined money supply average of M2 plus certificates of deposit (CDs) grew a preliminary 3.1 percent in January from a year earlier, the Bank of Japan (BOJ) said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>A breakdown of money supply figures follows:</p>
<p>(Year-on-year percentage changes)</p>
<p>			     JAN PRELIM   DEC REVISED NOV</p>
<p> Unadjusted M2 + CDs     +3.1	 +3.1     + 3.3</p>
<p>    M1			+10.3	+10.0     +10.8</p>
<p>    CDs		     +53.8	+34.4     +55.5</p>
<p>			     JAN PRELIM   DEC REVISED NOV</p>
<p> Broadest money measure  +3.6	 +3.6     + 3.6</p>
<p>(Annualised month-on-month percentage changes)</p>
<p>			     JAN PRELIM   DEC REVISED NOV</p>
<p> Adjusted M2 + CDs	 +3.2	 +1.7     + 2.8</p>
<p>(Average outstanding yen levels)</p>
<p>			   JAN PRELIM  DEC REVISED   NOV</p>
<p>Unadjusted M2+CDs   563.2 trln  566.3 trln 556.1 trln</p>
<p>    M1		  174.7 trln  177.9 trln 163.7 trln</p>
<p>    CDs		  16.0 trln   15.7 trln  16.2 trln</p>
<p>			   JAN PRELIM  DEC REVISED   NOV</p>
<p>Broadest liquidity 1,140.1 trln 1,139.6 trln1, 126.5 trln</p>
</text>
